.TH GROUPADD 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
groupadd \- create a new group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B groupadd
.I group
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create
.I group
in
.BR /etc/group ,
with a freshly allocated GID (the lowest unused id at or above 1000).
.SH SECURITY
.B This has not been independently security-reviewed.
Modifies
.B /etc/group
directly, under the same lock file
.RB ( /etc/.pwd.lock )
real shadow-utils uses. Read
.B common::accounts
in the source before installing this setuid anywhere that matters --
the same weight as
.BR su (1)/ sudo (1)'s
own SECURITY sections, for the same reason: a bug here can corrupt
the account database, not just misbehave for one user. Get it
reviewed and test it in a disposable VM first.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR, and \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the group already exists, the name is
invalid, or the database couldn't be locked/written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR useradd (1),
.BR passwd (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
